# The display attached to the IOMMU — patches 0051 + 0052, docs/vaapi-scope.md.
#
#   echo 0052-arm64-dts-h713-attach-the-display-to-the-iommu.patch \
#       >> patches/kernel/series
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=dispiommu build/build.sh kernel
#     -> build/out/h713-kernel-dispiommu.fit
#
# 0052 is NOT in `series` and must not be: it is an experiment that departs from
# the vendor configuration, and a plain `build/build.sh kernel` would otherwise
# ship it. Add the line, build, then take it out again. 0051 (rate-limit the
# fault print) *is* in the series -- it is a correctness fix on its own terms,
# and unrelated to whether the display is ever translated.
#
# This fragment deliberately changes NOTHING. It exists only so the build gets
# its own tree and its own FIT name and cannot overwrite the production one;
# the experiment itself is entirely in the two patches.
#
# In particular it does NOT set CONFIG_LOCALVERSION, unlike the other debug
# fragments here, and that is the point. Those build their drivers in because a
# renamed kernel has no module tree on the board. This one keeps `uname -r` at
# plain 6.18.38, so /lib/modules/6.18.38 — the in-tree drivers AND the
# out-of-tree aic8800 WiFi/BT modules — loads unchanged. That keeps the network
# up, which is what makes an hour-long soak observable over ssh instead of over
# a 115200-baud console, and it keeps the configuration bit-identical to the one
# the corruption was characterised on. Modules, not built-ins, so the DRM card
# numbering also stays as production: card0 panfrost, card1 AFBD.
#
# The cost is that `uname -r` cannot tell you which kernel booted. Check the
# build date in `dmesg | head -1`, or just confirm the experiment took:
#
#   dmesg | grep '5600000.display: Adding to iommu group'
#
# WHAT TO WATCH FOR, in order of how bad it is:
#
#   * a fault storm at boot that outruns the ratelimit -> the window between the
#     IOMMU attaching the device and the KMS driver programming an IOVA, while
#     the panel still fetches U-Boot's physical carveout. Expected if the panel
#     was brought up in U-Boot; it must stop once AFBD probes.
#   * "Page fault for <addr> (master 2, dir wr)" during the soak -> THE GOAL.
#     That is the display writing outside its mappings, named at last.
#   * a full hour of playback with no fault and no corruption -> also a result:
#     translation contains it, and the write was a device's.
#   * a full hour of playback with no fault and corruption anyway -> the most
#     informative outcome. No device on this IOMMU is doing it, so it is the
#     CPU, and a stale userspace mapping of a freed dumb buffer is next.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION=""
